      "writtenOn": "2024-06-17T11:00:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should be able to remove \"track_event_abi.h\" (included by \"track_event.h\"), and \"te_macros.h\" (not used here).\n\n* \"te_category_macros.h\" is already included by \"ServiceManager.h\", but I\u0027d still include it here, since we\u0027re using one of the macros.\n* \"producer.h\" is required for PerfettoProducerInit\n* \"track_event.h\" is required for PerfettoTeInit\n\n\u003e same for this - it\u0027s a lot of headers. Does every client need so many?\n\nIn general yes, multiple headers are required the idea is roughly:\n\n* In the main file of a process, you need to connect to perfetto. That lives in its own header (\"producer.h\")\n* In the main file of a process, you need to register the data sources that you\u0027re using. In this case, we\u0027re only using simple track event instrumentation, that requires \"track_event.h\" and \"te_category_macros.h\"\n* Every other file that\u0027s instrumented could only use \"te_macros.h\". We don\u0027t want to include \"producer.h\" from every file.",
      "parentUuid": "a7041933_121aaaa2",
